+# baske: Citra leaves THOUSANDS of .o files and the ar command came to ~57,000 characters,
+# far past Windows' ~32,768 limit: it failed with "Error 127", which misleads because it
+# sounds like a missing tool and the tool was right there. GNU ar takes a response file with
+# @file, but generating it with a shell command would hit the same ceiling; make's own
+# file-writing function (4.0+, here 4.4.1) does not go through the shell.
+# Two traps, each of which cost a round:
+#  - These comments are NOT indented. Indented they would be part of the recipe and make
+#    would expand whatever they carry (it failed with "invalid file operation").
+#  - Make expands the WHOLE recipe before running the first command, so the .rsp is written
+#    BEFORE any rm in the recipe. That is why it is not deleted here: if it were, ar would
+#    find the file already gone and would build an empty .a (8 bytes).
