+    // per page table (that is, per emulated process) on top of one per ARM11 core. On the
+    // Switch that is half a gigabyte of heap we do not have, plus as much again of code
+    // region for the executable alias. And there is worse than the memory: on Horizon no
+    // memory is writable and executable at once, so oaknut::CodeBlock flips the permissions
+    // of the WHOLE block with svcSetProcessMemoryPermission before and after emitting each
+    // basic block (see code_block.hpp). That syscall costs in proportion to the size: at the
+    // default it is 32768 pages per compiled block. 32 MiB is plenty for the 3DS -- dynarmic
+    // only flushes the cache when less than 1 MiB is left.
+    config.code_cache_size = 32 * 1024 * 1024;
+
     config.coprocessors[15] = std::make_shared<DynarmicCP15>(cp15_state);
     config.define_unpredictable_behaviour = true;
 
